    "result_text": "Full build is green. \n\nI implemented the daily-limit rule following the existing capacity-rule pattern, keeping structural impact minimal \u2014 I added small, cohesive new units rather than growing any existing class:\n\n- **`RejectOwnerDailyLimit`** (new function class, CC=2) \u2014 counts owners whose `registrationDate` is today and throws when the count reaches 100 (so the 101st is rejected), mirroring `RejectOwnerCityAtCapacity`.\n- **`DailyOwnerLimitException`** (new checked exception) and **`DailyOwnerLimitExceptionHandler`** (new handler \u2192 429 `TOO_MANY_REQUESTS`).\n- **Escalation YAML** mapping the exception to its handler.\n- **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 inserted one `rejectDailyLimit` step into the pipeline (the only existing file touched; it has no functions).\n\n`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS.",
